<<~ ahu #/intent>>
! Art Sigils — Procedure Vocabulary

Define structure once; feed all subjects, artists, histories, styles, materials, narrative relationships and visual hypotheses into calls. No Greek geography, genre, fixed artist, or default aesthetic belongs inside a reusable procedure. Keep all `\procedure` pragmas before ordinary WikiText content and calls. This document presents its procedure declarations together inside a fenced source block so its surrounding meme commentary does not masquerade as a directly importable procedure-definition tiddler. A pure-definition tiddler contains those declarations without surrounding commentary.

`\procedure` and `<<name parameter:"value">>` illustrate native TiddlyWiki5. Lares `<<~ name ...>>` follows a house convention, with no automatic native WikiText equivalence. Parameter calls below use short single-line strings to avoid assuming a parser handles multiline quoted arguments identically in every context.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/definitions>>
!! Reusable procedure definitions — source-only

```tiddlywiki
\procedure art-work(name kind purpose)
! <<name>>
Kind: <<kind>>
Purpose: <<purpose>>
\end art-work

\procedure art-address(audience relationship invitation)
Audience: <<audience>>
Relation: <<relationship>>
Invitation: <<invitation>>
\end art-address

\procedure art-depict(subject setting location)
Subject: <<subject>>
Setting: <<setting>>
Depiction-scope: <<location>>
\end art-depict

\procedure art-reference(artist contribution application)
Reference: <<artist>>
Contribution: <<contribution>>
Application: <<application>>
\end art-reference

\procedure art-read(first second third)
First read: <<first>>
Second read: <<second>>
Later discovery: <<third>>
\end art-read

\procedure art-contrast(left right relation)
Contrast: <<left>> / <<right>>
Visual effect: <<relation>>
\end art-contrast

\procedure art-place(element site action)
Element: <<element>>
Placement: <<site>>
Interaction: <<action>>
\end art-place

\procedure art-view(system spatial-rule limits)
View convention: <<system>>
Spatial behavior: <<spatial-rule>>
Limits: <<limits>>
\end art-view

\procedure art-study(question form proposal status)
Question: <<question>>
Study form: <<form>>
Proposal: <<proposal>>
Status: <<status>>
\end art-study

\procedure art-dispute(study-a study-b disagreement visible-proof)
Studies: <<study-a>> / <<study-b>>
Disagreement: <<disagreement>>
Visible evidence: <<visible-proof>>
\end art-dispute

\procedure art-media(support medium implement technique handling)
Support: <<support>>
Medium: <<medium>>
Implement: <<implement>>
Technique: <<technique>>
Handling: <<handling>>
\end art-media

\procedure art-edge(region contour contrast detail)
Region: <<region>>
Edge: <<contour>>
Contrast: <<contrast>>
Detail: <<detail>>
\end art-edge

\procedure art-light(region source color effect)
Region: <<region>>
Light source: <<source>>
Colour treatment: <<color>>
Effect: <<effect>>
\end art-light

\procedure art-withhold(region absence purpose)
Region: <<region>>
Withhold: <<absence>>
Purpose: <<purpose>>
\end art-withhold

\procedure art-history(layer evidence interpretation)
Historical layer: <<layer>>
Visible evidence: <<evidence>>
Interpretation: <<interpretation>>
\end art-history

\procedure art-boundary(scope preserve undecided)
Scope: <<scope>>
Preserve: <<preserve>>
Open questions: <<undecided>>
\end art-boundary

\procedure art-observe(region feature relation)
Region: <<region>>
Observed feature: <<feature>>
Visible relation: <<relation>>
\end art-observe

\procedure art-infer(interpretation evidence alternative)
Interpretation: <<interpretation>>
Evidence: <<evidence>>
Alternative: <<alternative>>
\end art-infer

\procedure art-critique(effect problem suggestion)
Effect: <<effect>>
Concern: <<problem>>
Possible adjustment: <<suggestion>>
\end art-critique
```
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/sample-calls>>
!! Generic invocations — examples of replacing *all* black-ink content

```tiddlywiki
<<art-work name:"Unfinished River Port" kind:"environment exploration drawing" purpose:"Investigate the navigability of a flooded industrial waterfront">>
<<art-address audience:"level designer" relationship:"review of route alternatives" invitation:"compare uncertain crossings rather than admire a finished promotional scene">>
<<art-depict subject:"waterfront warehouses and boats" setting:"flooded estuary at dusk" location:"inside the drawn environment; no external reviewer depicted">>
<<art-reference artist:"an identified cartographer" contribution:"legible river terrace form" application:"separate the navigable channel from submerged streets">>
<<art-dispute study-a:"ink flood map" study-b:"painterly skyline" disagreement:"a raised causeway blocks the pictured boat route" visible-proof:"erased route and corrected waterline on translucent overlay">>
<<art-media support:"smooth white Bristol" medium:"brown ink" implement:"dip nib" technique:"sparse hatching" handling:"one erased pencil guide remains under the finished contour">>
<<art-withhold region:"far bank" absence:"dense architectural detail" purpose:"preserve atmosphere and make the navigation problem readable">>
```

The sample demonstrates topic substitution without embedding the river-port in the definitions. A new Example Zero retains whichever references the operator explicitly locks; no other thematic defaults travel silently.
<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu #/craft-notes>>
!! Disciplined use

* Favor art-critical verbs in param names: `contrast`, `withhold`, `observe`, `infer`, `dispute`, `place`, `read`.
* Keep `audience` and `depiction-scope` distinct. An external critic or director does not become a figure in the scene.
* Give nested images individual study scopes. Physical paper, applied media, and depicted materials must not share an invented universal tooth.
* A study exists to answer or contest a question; distinguish deliberate unfinishedness from accidental incompleteness.
* Avoid an exhaustive ontology of commands. A few meaningful primitives support varied formal and informal language.
* Retain uncertainty explicitly for unconfirmed source materials, techniques, intentions and mythological identities.
* In a native procedure-definition tiddler, place pragmas before content and calls; arrange surrounding metadata according to its container. These examples express an authoring vocabulary, not an execution claim.
<<~/ahu>>

